-- status  : Open
-- author  : @mikedeng1
-- created : 2026-10-07T07:50:36.35114+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/02110a8d-7a4d-409a-a676-0f104189b3d2
-- title:
--   Theorem 2.1, p. 4 — |v(ξ) − v(ξ̃)| ≤ L(‖ξ − ξ̃‖_r + Σ_{t=2}^{T−1} D_t(F_t, F̃_t))
-- statement:
--   Consider the linear multistage stochastic program (1) with input process $\xi = (\xi_1,\dots,\xi_T)$, polyhedral $X_1$, polyhedral cones $X_t$ ($t \ge 2$), fixed recourse matrices, and costs $b_t$ and right-hand sides $h_t$ affine in $\xi_t$, under one of the three randomness patterns with exponents $(r,r')$. Assume
--
--   1. (A1) complete fixed recourse: $A_{t,0}X_t = \mathbb R^{n_t}$ for $t = 2,\dots,T$;
--   2. (A2) $v(\xi)$ is finite and the objective $F$ is level-bounded locally uniformly at $\xi$;
--   3. (A3) $\xi \in L_r(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mathbb P;\mathbb R^{Td})$, with $\xi_1$ deterministic;
--   4. $X_1$ is bounded.
--
--   Then there are positive constants $L$, $\alpha$, $\delta$ such that
--   $$|v(\xi) - v(\tilde\xi)| \le L\Big( \|\xi - \tilde\xi\|_r + \sum_{t=2}^{T-1} D_t(\mathcal F_t, \tilde{\mathcal F}_t) \Big)$$
--   for every admissible input $\tilde\xi$ with $\|\tilde\xi - \xi\|_r \le \delta$ and $v(\tilde\xi)$ finite. Here $\mathcal F_t$ and $\tilde{\mathcal F}_t$ are the filtrations generated by $\xi$ and $\tilde\xi$, and
--   $$D_t(\mathcal F_t,\tilde{\mathcal F}_t) = \max\Big\{ \sup_{x \in l_\alpha(F(\xi,\cdot))} \|x_t - \mathbb E[x_t \mid \tilde{\mathcal F}_t]\|_{r'},\ \sup_{\tilde x \in l_\alpha(F(\tilde\xi,\cdot))} \|\tilde x_t - \mathbb E[\tilde x_t \mid \mathcal F_t]\|_{r'} \Big\},$$
--   both level sets taken at threshold $v(\xi) + \alpha$.
--
--   The theorem shows that the optimal value of a multistage program depends on the input not only through an $L_r$ distance but also through a distance between the information structures, and that the two together control it in a Lipschitz way.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The estimate is stated in $[0,\infty]$ (`ENNReal.ofReal |v(ξ) − v(ξ̃)| ≤ …`); both optimal values are finite extended reals, so their real parts are the values themselves. The randomness pattern is a hypothesis on the data, and all three rows of the paper's table are covered. Admissible inputs are measurable, in $L_r$, and have a deterministic first component, as the model's $\mathcal F_1 = \{\emptyset,\Omega\}$ requires.
-- source:
--   Heitsch, Römisch & Strugarek, Stability of multistage stochastic programs, author manuscript (edoc.hu-berlin.de, c. 2005), pp. 4–5, Theorem 2.1, (8)–(9)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MultistageStab_Value_Setting

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal

namespace MultistageStab.Value

theorem theorem_2_1 (D : Data) (pat : Pattern) (hpat : pat.Holds D)
    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (ξ : ℕ → Ω → E D.d) (hA1 : CompleteRecourse D) (hA2 : A2 P D pat ξ)
    (hA3 : Admissible P D pat ξ) (hX1 : Bornology.IsBounded (X1 D)) :
    ∃ L : ℝ, 0 < L ∧ ∃ α : ℝ, 0 < α ∧ ∃ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ ∧
      ∀ ξ' : ℕ → Ω → E D.d, Admissible P D pat ξ' →
        inputDist P D pat ξ ξ' ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ →
        value P D pat ξ' ≠ ⊥ → value P D pat ξ' ≠ ⊤ →
        ENNReal.ofReal |(value P D pat ξ).toReal - (value P D pat ξ').toReal| ≤
          ENNReal.ofReal L * (inputDist P D pat ξ ξ' +
            ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 2 (D.T - 1), filtDist P D pat ξ ξ' α t) := by sorry

end MultistageStab.Value
